@startuml account-lifecycle
!theme plain
title Agent account lifecycle (one generation; generations are never reused)

[*] --> creating : user.create\n(under the helper lock: allocate UID/GID,\nledger entry, journal)
creating --> active : account, group and home created\n(v1: egress denial installed first)
creating --> [*] : failure or crash →\nrolled back by recovery
active --> active : launch.start (launcher)\nfw.apply (v1)
active --> retiring : user.retire\n(commit point: persisted first)
retiring --> retiring : processes remain →\nretry later (removal only moves forward)
retiring --> removed : launcher and broker refuse the generation;\nprocesses stopped and verified;\nhome quarantined, archived or deleted;\naccount, group, then rules removed
removed --> [*]
note right of retiring
  from here the launcher refuses new starts,
  the broker refuses leases,
  and crash recovery resumes forward
end note
@enduml
